  "body": "An inch document's refusals still read millimeters: a bore 25 mm too deep was refused as `25.000 mm deep`, a `Ø14 shank in a Ø12 hole` quoted bare millimeters - while every dialog around it spoke inches (#740).\n\n## The change\n\nThe refusal sentences are built deep in the generator, off the worker threads, world-free - that's why they never saw the document's unit. The fix carries the unit to them rather than reaching for the world:\n\n- `GenJob` grows a `unit: Unit` field; `collect_job` fills it from `crate::units::of(world)` while the world is still in hand, and it rides into every refusal builder as one added argument (`too_deep`, `shank_fits`, `axial_reach`, the cross-reach family in `cross_spindle`/`cross_stock`/`cross_holder`, `circle_of_region`, `pocket_region_on_part`/`around_part`, `offset_run`). `AreaCtx` carries it the same way.\n- The lens itself: `units::len(v_mm, unit, prec)` prints `{:.prec}` byte-identically in millimeters and the converted value at `prec + 2` in inches; `Unit::suffix()` gives the word. Every pinned number is `{:.3}` in mm, so inch refusals read five decimals. Where the sentence had a literal `\" mm\"` it now ends `units::len(..) + unit.suffix()`; bare numbers (mouth coordinates, `shank dia. {:.3}`, `Z {:.3}`) become suffixless `units::len(..)`.\n- `GenError::At`'s location stays millimeters - the lens is for the sentence, not the geometry marker. Tests pin this.\n- Two `#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]` attrs (`axial_reach`, `shank_fits`), following the existing convention in `generate.rs`/`plunge_solid.rs`.\n\nMillimeter documents change not one byte: the existing suite, which pins these sentences verbatim, passes untouched.\n\n## Pins (red on main, green with the fix)\n\n`crates/app/tests/units_in_refusals.rs` runs five operations twice each, mm then inch, asserting the mm sentence byte-for-byte and the inch sentence converted:\n\n- `an_axial_reach_refusal_speaks_the_document_unit` - through-hole `too_deep`: depth, flute, fix depth cross the lens, ` mm` becomes ` in`.\n- `a_cross_reach_refusal_speaks_the_document_unit` - raw-bar cross hole: mouth coords `(10.000, 0.000, 0.000)` -> `(0.39370, 0.00000, 0.00000)`; the `At` location is pinned to stay `(10, 0, 0)` mm.\n- `a_shank_fit_refusal_speaks_the_document_unit` - the BR-1000 shank refusal: depth/flute lensed, bare `shank dia. 14.000` -> `0.55118`; location pinned mm.\n- `a_circle_fit_refusal_speaks_the_document_unit` - circular-fit deviation and centre point.\n- `a_part_fills_the_selection_refusal_speaks_the_document_unit` - the plane named in the area refusal: ` at Z 7.000` -> ` at Z 0.27559`.\n\n## Scope, relative to the claim table\n\n- `material::section()`'s refusal is dead code - dropped.\n- The `holder()` raw-`Display` refusal and the pure-crate refusals (`camcraft-tools`, `camcraft-motion`) need their unit plumbed through crate APIs, not job args - a follow-up PR.\n- Refusals quoting profile constants (`spun`, `holder_profile`, `lathe_holder`) quote tool definitions, not document measurements - left alone.\n- The contour travel *note* (`contour: rides the open boundary 0.400 mm...`) is a note, not a refusal - left for the same follow-up.\n\n## Tested\n\n- Red first: with only the pins committed, `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test units_in_refusals` builds clean and all five fail on the millimeter strings they still see.\n- Green: same command, 5 passed, 0 failed.\n- The mm byte-identity proof: untouched sentence pins across the drilling/area/pick suites all pass unmodified - lib `drill_reach` (8), `area::` (4), `contour_open` (2), and integration binaries `drill_reach`, `drill_reach_fit`, `drilling_cross_holder`, `drilling_cross_spindle`, `drilling_cross_stock`, `drilling_cross_rapids`, `drilling_axial`, `circular_pick`, `pick_agnostic`, `drilling_cross`, `drilling_cross_box`, `drilling_cross_part`, `drill_prior`, `drill_prior_kinds`, `drill_rplane`, `lathe_cross_drill`, `area_controls`, `area_open`, `area_picks`, `whole_model_pocket`, `boundary_walls`, `probe_pick`, `refusal_location`, `pick`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` finishes clean.\n- Not exercised: the other crates - the fix touches only `camcraft-app`.\n\nChangelog: generator refusals now print their numbers in the document's unit - an inch document reads inches, millimeter documents unchanged (#740)\n\nFixes #740\n",
